From: UTDeck
Subject: [PATCH] services: keep the x86 translator choice (HODLL, HODLL64) for services

services.exe starts each service with an environment made from the registry (CreateEnvironmentBlock),
and only WINEBOOTSTRAPMODE is copied over from its own. HODLL (the translator wow64 loads for 32-bit
x86 code: wowbox64.dll, Hangover's default, or libwow64fex.dll) and HODLL64 (ntdll's, for x86-64
code) are lost there, so a service and every program it starts get the default, whatever the game's
setting says.

The EA app's background service (EABackgroundService.exe) starts Microsoft's Visual C++ 2012 x86
installer at every game start until it is installed. Under Box64 its WiX "burn" engine waits at full
CPU forever (as Steam's Visual C++ 2015 installer did in stage 3.S); the game's FEX setting
(HODLL=libwow64fex.dll) did not reach it, and the game's prefix stayed up after the game was quit
(Need for Speed Most Wanted 2012 on our base, the Nothing Phone (1), stage 4.10).

Both names are now kept as WINEBOOTSTRAPMODE is.
---
diff --git a/programs/services/services.c b/programs/services/services.c
--- a/programs/services/services.c
+++ b/programs/services/services.c
@@ -1033,15 +1033,25 @@
 
     if (!environment && OpenProcessToken(GetCurrentProcess(), TOKEN_QUERY | TOKEN_DUPLICATE, &token))
     {
-        WCHAR val[16];
+        /* UTDeck: HODLL and HODLL64 (the x86 translator wow64 and ntdll load) are kept too, so a
+         * service and the programs it starts use the game's choice, not the default (Box64). */
+        static const WCHAR *const kept[] = { L"WINEBOOTSTRAPMODE", L"HODLL", L"HODLL64" };
+        WCHAR val[MAX_PATH];
+        unsigned int i;
+
         CreateEnvironmentBlock(&environment, token, FALSE);
-        if (GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"WINEBOOTSTRAPMODE", val, ARRAY_SIZE(val) ))
+        for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(kept); i++)
         {
-            UNICODE_STRING name = RTL_CONSTANT_STRING(L"WINEBOOTSTRAPMODE");
-            UNICODE_STRING value;
+            DWORD len = GetEnvironmentVariableW( kept[i], val, ARRAY_SIZE(val) );
+
+            if (len && len < ARRAY_SIZE(val))
+            {
+                UNICODE_STRING name, value;
 
-            RtlInitUnicodeString( &value, val );
-            RtlSetEnvironmentVariable( (WCHAR **)&environment, &name, &value );
+                RtlInitUnicodeString( &name, kept[i] );
+                RtlInitUnicodeString( &value, val );
+                RtlSetEnvironmentVariable( (WCHAR **)&environment, &name, &value );
+            }
         }
         CloseHandle(token);
     }
